A||||19||BlackStang95||Fiero Crash||||9||
Z||000000||BlackStang95||11-08-2001||05:21 PM||||Me and Spektrum were cruising in his fiero (silver 87 gt) last night after a trip to the gym, there's this road through a local industrial park thats got a series of twists and curves.  We've drove through it before, usually in his car, i raced a maxima down it once.  Earlier in the night we were talking about how the fiero handles and all.  So anyway he started taking the curves really fast, and i was thinking whens he gonna brake and then he accelerated, he was going 75-80 in a 35, the back end just went out and next thing we hit the curb backwards, skidded down it for about 100 feet, smoke and sparks everywhere, we come to rest on the grass a few feet from trees.  Luckily theres no one around so he tries to get outta there befoer cops or anyone come, backs off the 6 inch curb again, and then realizes he cant steer, so in order to egt it out of the middle of the road plows head on over the curb again.  Then we walk about 2 miles to a 7-11 where he calls his parents,  they come pick us up and he gets the car towed to a repair place in the morning.  He manages to avoid any police charges, very lucky, and the repair place estimates $618 to fix.  Definitely came away from that good, hes getting new steering, front cv joints, tire, etc, basically everything under the car.  So, we came away good, defintely will be no more thinking the fiero is invincible, driving crazy etc i hope.  Just thought I'd share this story with the forum  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">.||||reg||9
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||11-08-2001||06:26 PM||||Like I tell my son, the back-end is solid right up to the point that it slips.<BR>Once it slips, it's GONE!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Master_Sushi||11-08-2001||06:32 PM||||That sure sucks the big one. The accidents that always feel the worst are the ones that could have been avoided with more careful driving. Only important thing is that nobody got hurt. Fieros don’t cost that much to replace and its a lesson learned.<P>Best of luck to both of you!<P><BR>{edited for typo}<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Master_Sushi (edited 11-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mach10||11-08-2001||06:44 PM||||hehehe... Similar thing happened to me... Just out of the carwash, carrying a large chocolate sundae to eat at work... Hammered it hard going onto the street, whipped around the turnoff a little quick... This was back when I first had the car, and didn't know how to drive it properly. Back end flew out, I overcorrected, and ended up doing a full 360, narrowly missing both curbs. Unfortunately, the sundae had left the cup, and was now splattered in alternating streaks (left-right) all over my interior... D-OH!||||reg||10
Z||000004||Spektrum-87GT||11-08-2001||08:42 PM||||please just let this thread die, i dont want to talk about it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Mach10||11-08-2001||08:46 PM||||hehehehe... At least YOU got some damage out of it... I was covered head-toe in chocolate sauce and ice-cream... You can make excuses about road conditions, or pretend it didn't happen... I had to go back to work with no change of clothes  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Sorry to hear it, though... Really sucks when the car takes a hit. At least no-one was hurt. Are you insured?||||reg||10
