Z||000007||Formula88||11-08-2001||09:05 PM||||That sucks, man - but glad no one was hurt.  Yeah, Fiero's have really high limits, but when you reach those limits, they are a bear to hang on to!  Go past the limits, and it's almost impossible to get the car back in control.<P>No one ever said 911's were easy to drive, either.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||Master_Sushi||11-08-2001||09:09 PM||||$hit happens! Everybody screws up smashes a car up once and a while, its not that uncommon. I've had a few close calls while driveing my fiero(s). I won't go into them, most were my fault though.<P>Dosen't sound like you totaled it or anything. 600$ isn't that bad or a repair bill(if you had an 88 you'd be screwed lol). Insurance didn't find out about it so you don't have to worry about that.<BR>From what happend things sound to have turned out pretty well...<P>GL||||reg||1
Z||000009||Spektrum-87GT||11-08-2001||09:35 PM||||liability only, 600 out of pocket... not bad at all considering what happened. I'm getting a new steering rack too, a lot of new front end parts, a suspension overhaul, and most importantly no one was hurt. The fiero didnt have any body or frame damage luckly. I couldnt sleep last night, but I'm very happy that I will once again have my fiero back in hopefully close to the same shape, if not better with all the new parts. Cheap, yet stressful lesson learned that speed is dangerous and it should be kept on the track. I was supposed to go on a date this weekend too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000010||Mach10||11-08-2001||09:38 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Spektrum-87GT:<BR><B>liability only, 600 out of pocket... not bad at all considering what happened. I'm getting a new steering rack too, a lot of new front end parts, a suspension overhaul, and most importantly no one was hurt. The fiero didnt have any body or frame damage luckly. I couldnt sleep last night, but I'm very happy that I will once again have my fiero back in hopefully close to the same shape, if not better with all the new parts. Cheap, yet stressful lesson learned that speed is dangerous and it should be kept on the track. I was supposed to go on a date this weekend too   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>And therein is the absolute benefit of government-monopolized public insurance. No such thing as "liability only," and I'm pretty sure that I pay less for my 50k damage, 500k liability 200 deductible than you do for liability only   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>That REALLY sucks, dude. <P>||||reg||9
Z||000011||FieroMaster88||11-08-2001||09:40 PM||||I did something like that with my first car.  It was a 89 buick century with a 2.5L.  I was driving too fast in the rain, tried to turn a corner and she just plowed.  Right over the curb.  I ended up having to pay a $740 repair bill.  Some of us have to learn the hard way!  I am glad you guys were ok! <P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jamessig.jpg">                   <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>Not your ordinary 88 coupe!||||reg||1
Z||000012||FieroKyle||11-08-2001||11:24 PM||||I know how that is, I did exactly the same thing, except I was doing about 90. I have taken the corner at 85 and made it stick before, but I decided to push it. It pushed back. Back end started coming on around and broke loose faster than fast. Ended of backing into a few inches tall cement gaurd rail. Didn't do any body damage, but it did bent up my exhaust pretty good. I was able to bend it back though. I did that in June, the skid marks are still there.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I dunno, Fierowrecker might have seen them, it happened a half mile from his house.||||reg||1
Z||000013||pHoOl||11-08-2001||11:49 PM||||Damn dude, what curve were you taking at 85 successfully?  i don't know if i'd even think about attemting that.  You'll have to show me the curve sometime.<P>------------------<BR>Kills:<BR>97 Neon R/T<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>         <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/phoolsig2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||FieroGTChile87||11-09-2001||12:58 AM||||I came close once. I hammered it halfway through this one really long wind and the rear sort of hopped and chirped the tires but, luckily it went back into place when I let off the throttle. I wouldn't have known what to do if it would have went and, right next to me was a guard rail with a really big cliff and it was in the middle of nowhere.<P>------------------<BR>Maroon 87 GT<BR>Gold 87 SE V6 (Disabled)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroGTChile_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
